From bf0c2667d17fd1417d402df146d70aa1e6758cfb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 07:20:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Gate sync parent evidence on changed task rows

Reuse trusted local and shadow P2 cursors for the foreign-parent mirror.
Update affected rows and children of changed parents, retaining fail-closed
full reads and a 30-second mirror recovery floor. Keep all existing repair
and heal passes, freshness stamps and attachment due-time selection.
Batch attachment retry stamps and avoid unchanged metadata transactions;
preserve first-transfer and failed-retry priority ordering.

Proof: RED real-round idle/floor and changed task/run/event assertions, then
GREEN focused integration, scope, attachment and repair suites. Code-health
check passes. Prior checkpoint/endpoint experiments and benchmark harnesses
are intentionally not in this narrowed change. CPU budget is NOT claimed:
exact-head review/CI, updater deployment and same-PID P1 remain required.
